.eslintcache

# release/ (the whole extension) is intentionally committed: it is the folder
# `Load unpacked` selects, and has to work from a clean clone. `npm run check:build` guards
# against it drifting from src/.

# Personal, machine-local Claude Code overrides (permission grants and the
# like). Deliberately untracked: committing it would apply one developer's
# permission grants to everyone who clones the repo. Shared project-level
# settings belong in .claude/settings.json instead.
.claude/settings.local.json
